# surface: idol
# NEGATIVE CONTROL for G-TOTAL, and the positive control for the diagnostic
# path. Every marked span below has TWO candidates and no surface fact that
# separates them, so the projector must DIAGNOSE rather than default. A gate
# reporting "0 unresolved spans" over a corpus that cannot produce one is the
# kind of zero §3 says is usually a broken gate; this file is what stops that.
#
# A leading `.` at the head of a clause: §0.3 reads it as an inferred case,
# §0a reads it as a field of the subject. Both are law. Nothing on the line
# decides, so nothing may be coloured.
.eof
# THE SEMICOLON DOES NOT EXIST. A byte spelling one names no edge.
n = 1;
# And the space walk where the surface CANNOT decide: is `i` a descriptor or a
# place? Two candidates, no rule between them, so both brackets diagnose.
q = xs[i]
